# Lean build context for the dashboard image.
#
# The build context is the PLUGIN ROOT (the launcher pins it via
# Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent — i.e. this dir), so it also contains
# commands/, agents/, skills/, workflows/, references/, plugin.json, and the rest
# of scripts/.
#
# Strategy: deny everything, then re-include ONLY the runtime paths the image
# needs. This guarantees the plugin's commands/agents/skills/workflows, docs,
# tests, the other scripts (dashboard_launcher.py, run_state.py, worktrees.py,
# quality_gate.py, …), and __pycache__ never enter the build context — nothing
# but the server, the two pure cores it imports, and the baked UI assets is
# available to COPY.
#
# This list must stay in sync with the Dockerfile's COPY lines: a path the
# Dockerfile copies but this file does not re-include is simply absent from the
# context, and the build fails on that COPY.
*

# Re-include only the runtime files (NOT a blanket !scripts/, which would readmit
# tests and unrelated tooling). Docker needs the directory entries re-included so
# the traversal reaches the files below.
!scripts
scripts/*
!scripts/dashboard_server.py
!scripts/dag.py
!scripts/run_metrics.py
!scripts/dashboard_assets
scripts/dashboard_assets/*
!scripts/dashboard_assets/**

# Never ship test files even from a re-included directory.
scripts/dashboard_assets/*.test.mjs
